course: dictionary
lesson: 4624
title: Context clues: words about faith and clothing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things from a faith or a culture. You can often work out their meaning from the words around them. «A boy in Arizona made fun of a classmate's hijab (a Muslim headscarf) every day.» The brackets give the meaning straight away: a hijab is a headscarf.
explain: Look at the other clues too. A hijab covers the hair and neck but leaves the face open. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a Muslim headscarf every day" still makes sense, so you have checked it.
explain: Some words are about what people believe, so we use them with respect. The school treated the teasing as bullying, and the boy was suspended. Using a word about someone's faith to tease them is never okay.
fact: A hijab is a headscarf worn by many Muslim women and girls.
fact: A hijab covers the hair and neck and leaves the face open.
fact: Hijab can also mean the wider idea in Islam of dressing modestly.
fact: Schools often have hijabs in uniform colours, called a school hijab.
fact: Making fun of someone's hijab is bullying, and schools can act on it.
exercise: «A boy in Arizona made fun of a classmate's hijab (a Muslim headscarf) every day.» What is a hijab? | *A headscarf worn by many Muslim women and girls | A type of school bag | A sports shoe | A kind of sun hat
exercise: A hijab covers the hair and the neck. Which part is left open? | The neck | The hands | The hair | *The face
exercise: «The school treated it as bullying and the boy was suspended.» What did the school do? | It gave the boy a prize | *It treated the teasing as bullying and suspended the boy | It did nothing at all | It said the hijab was funny
test: The word hijab can also mean dressing modestly, as part of Islam. Which idea is that? | Running fast in a race | Cooking a big meal | *Dressing modestly, as part of Islam | Reading aloud in class
test: Why is teasing someone about their hijab wrong? | It is a fun game | *It is bullying and it hurts a classmate | It makes the teacher laugh | It only matters at home
exam: «Ella's team wore school hijabs in their team's colours.» What is a school hijab most likely to be? | A pair of football boots | A school bus | A kind of pencil case | *A headscarf in school uniform colours
